      <title>Economists Can't Predict the US Jobs Report With Confidence Anymore</title>
      <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/opinion/articles/2026-11-06/economists-can-t-predict-the-us-jobs-report-with-confidence-anymore</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">95ccd3c78c397d0c9c9bfc70</guid>
      <pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 19:00:23 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>Yet again, the economic soothsayers couldn’t have been more wrong about the latest report on the state of the US labor market released Friday, adding to a mounting string of errant forecasts and raising an obvious question: Why do the people who make a living forecasting one of the most important data points in the whole economy get it so wrong so often?</description>
