    <item>
      <title>Ph.D.s Making $800,000 Distort the Value of the Degree</title>
      <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/opinion/articles/2026-11-06/ph-d-s-making-800-000-distort-the-value-of-the-degree</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">6aad31b241b89701b012925f</guid>
      <pubDate>Fri, 06 Nov 2026 13:00:33 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>Getting a Ph.D. is the best thing I did for my career; it was also the worst experience of my life. No job I have had since required the degree. But it was still necessary; it taught me to think critically, cultivated my curiosity and conveyed a depth of understanding of the economy and financial markets that served me well. It also gave me confidence in my expertise: How many other people have spent years alone in a library solving a single math problem? Does that justify six years of my life?</description>
      <dc:creator>Allison Schrager</dc:creator>
